<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abhira people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Abhiras</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Abhiras were a pastoral people of western and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a> and inscriptions. Abhira chiefs served as generals under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-satraps">Western Satraps</a>, and in the 3rd century CE one of them, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishvarasena">Ishvarasena</a>, founded a kingdom around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nashik">Nashik</a> as Satavahana power declined. The Ahir community has traditionally been linked with them.</p></div>
